# Milestone: M6
# Covers: Phase 4 atom proto stubs — Boolean / Integer / Float / String
# / nil / void protos exist as realm globals; .clone() works through
# atom-method dispatch.
#
# Three things tested end-to-end:
#   1. atom-clone short-circuit (S-atom-clone-perf): for non-UVAL_OBJECT
#      receivers, .clone() returns the receiver value directly.
#   2. Wave-1 family-specific methods: Boolean.toString(), String.length().
#   3. Realm globals are reachable: Boolean / Integer / String / Nil / Void
#      each resolve to their atom proto singleton.

# Atom-clone returns self (S-atom-clone-perf).
1.clone()
[00000000] 1
true.clone()
[00000001] true
"foo".clone()
[00000002] "foo"

# String.length via atom-method dispatch.
"hello".length()
[00000003] 5

# Boolean.toString
true.toString()
[00000004] "true"
false.toString()
[00000005] "false"

# Realm globals reachable as protos.
Boolean == Boolean
[00000006] true
Integer == Integer
[00000007] true
String == String
[00000008] true
